e summary.<|end|><|start|>assistant<|channel|>final<|message|>**Summary (2‑3 sentences)**  \nSyllepte viridivertex is a moth species in the Crambidae family, first described by William Schaus in 1920. It is native to Venezuela, has an approximate wingspan of 30 mm, and its wings are brownish‑grey with distinct dark lines and post‑/antemedial markings. The Wikipedia page provides its taxonomic classification, a brief morphological description, and references, and notes that the article is currently a stub.<|return|>"
